    "title": "feat: store git merge-base during force-push operations",
    "body": "Keep a record of the current merge-base of the old head \u0026 new head during a force push to an open pull request.\r\n\r\nThis allows us to accurately `git range-diff` in the future to see the changes made during this force push, allowing the implementation of #5357 (when a design is ready).  A future `range-diff` implementation will need to compare the commits between \"merge-base of the old branch\" to the \"head of the old branch\", versus the commits between \"merge-base of the new branch\" to the \"head of the new branch\".  Without the merge-base recorded at the time the force push is made, if the base branch of the PR changed, or the base branch was force pushed, or the new commit was merged into the base branch, we wouldn't be able to compute the same commit IDs.\r\n\r\nThe merge bases are recorded into the comment table's `content` field, which is already used to record the force push's commit IDs.  The new `force_push` field is:\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n    \"is_force_push\": true,\r\n    \"commit_ids\": [\r\n        \"a4b8fe8109ac8220e2e38c3a1d81973b5fe1dee7\",\r\n        \"b49c37670769fd82192fb6f954abd680ad007da9\"\r\n    ],\r\n    \"force_push\": {\r\n        \"old_mb\": \"d348ec4c374e27aed5fc1878c729734298170445\",\r\n        \"new_mb\": \"d348ec4c374e27aed5fc1878c729734298170445\"\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nFuture additions will need to be aware that this information won't be populated for all force pushes, only new ones after this PR is implemented.\r\n\r\n### Compliance\r\n\r\n- [x] I confirm that I make this contribution in accordance with [Forgejo's AI Agreement](https://codeberg.org/forgejo/governance/src/commit/9084720dc6a7fbf1d3f358919d46bd6adfb55287/AIAgreement.md).\r\n\r\n### Tests for Go changes\r\n\r\n- I added test coverage for Go changes...\r\n  - [ ] in their respective `*_test.go` for unit tests.\r\n  - [x] in the `tests/integration` directory if it involves interactions with a live Forgejo server.\r\n- I ran...\r\n  - [x] `make pr-go` before pushing\r\n\r\n### Documentation\r\n\r\n- [ ] I created a pull request [to the documentation](https://codeberg.org/forgejo/docs) to explain to Forgejo users how to use this change.\r\n- [x] I did not document these changes and I do not expect someone else to do it.\r\n\r\n### Release notes\r\n\r\n- [ ] This change will be noticed by a Forgejo user or admin (feature, bug fix, performance, etc.). I suggest to include a release note for this change.\r\n- [x] This change is not visible to a Forgejo user or admin (refactor, dependency upgrade, etc.). I think there is no need to add a release note for this change.\r\n\r\n",
